# =============================================================================
# Workload Gateway box configuration — copy to .env and fill in.
# =============================================================================
# .env is gitignored, and it is the ONE file an operator writes: nothing
# committed is edited, so the box runs from an unmodified checkout. Five files
# are rendered from it by ./render.sh: connector.toml, operator-bearer.token,
# operator-write.keys, nginx/conf.d/node.conf and dns-01.env.
# docker-compose.yml reads the rest directly.
#
# Required lines with no value below are yours to fill. The block marked
# "THE TOON DEVNET PRESET" is filled already, with the devnet's values; keep it
# to join the devnet, or replace it as a whole to settle elsewhere.

# ── Required: who this gateway is ────────────────────────────────────────────

# This gateway's own ILP address. The connector answers for it ([node]), and
# the one route it terminates hangs off it: a tenant seals its handover to
# <ILP_ADDRESS>.handover. No default: pick one of your own, e.g.
# g.<your-name>.workload-gateway. render.sh refuses anything under `g.toon.` —
# the TOON fleet's own namespace — unless TOON_DEVNET_BOX=1, below.
ILP_ADDRESS=

# The gateway's domain. EVERY single label under it is a workload hostname:
# `<canonical label>.${GATEWAY_DOMAIN}` where the label is the 52-character
# lowercase base32 of the workload id, plus any readable `name` a handover
# asked for. Two DNS records point here:
#
#   ${GATEWAY_DOMAIN}     A -> this box
#   *.${GATEWAY_DOMAIN}   A -> this box
#
# The wildcard is not optional. Nobody can enumerate the labels in advance, so
# there is no per-name record to create and no per-name certificate to issue —
# which is why this box, alone in the fleet, validates over DNS-01.
# e.g. gw.example.com (the devnet box's is gw.devnet.toonprotocol.dev)
GATEWAY_DOMAIN=

# The hostname of this gateway's OWN ILP edge — where a tenant pays for a
# Gateway Handover. It MUST NOT be under GATEWAY_DOMAIN: a name there is a name
# a tenant can no longer be handed. ./render.sh refuses one that is.
#
#   ${EDGE_HOST}          A -> this box
#
# e.g. proxy.gateway.example.com (the devnet box's is
# proxy.gateway.devnet.toonprotocol.dev)
EDGE_HOST=

# Where Let's Encrypt sends expiry warnings.
LETSENCRYPT_EMAIL=you@example.com

# Leave at 1 until you have seen a staging certificate issue cleanly, then set
# 0 and re-run ./init-letsencrypt.sh. Staging certificates are untrusted by
# browsers but do not burn the production rate limit — and this box's
# certificate covers a wildcard, which is exactly the kind you do not want to
# spend five attempts on.
LETSENCRYPT_STAGING=1

# ── Required: DNS-01 ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# A wildcard is issued over DNS-01 only, so certbot must be able to write a TXT
# record in the zone that holds GATEWAY_DOMAIN. DNS_PROVIDER picks the hook
# that does it — certbot/<DNS_PROVIDER>.py — and that hook reads its
# credentials from the <PROVIDER>_* lines below. render.sh hands the certbot
# container DNS_PROVIDER and those lines and nothing else; no key is ever
# printed. Shipped: porkbun, cloudflare. Another provider is one new file under
# certbot/ (README.md § "DNS-01"), and its lines go here the same way.
#
# Fill the block for your provider and leave the other commented out. The
# zone is the REGISTERED domain, not a subdomain: `gw.example.com` is not a
# zone, `example.com` is.
DNS_PROVIDER=

# Porkbun: an API key pair, with API access switched on for the domain.
# PORKBUN_ZONE=example.com
# PORKBUN_API_KEY=
# PORKBUN_SECRET_KEY=

# Cloudflare: an API TOKEN (not the global key) from the "Edit zone DNS"
# template, scoped to this one zone. CLOUDFLARE_ZONE_ID is optional and skips
# the zone lookup.
# CLOUDFLARE_ZONE=example.com
# CLOUDFLARE_API_TOKEN=
# CLOUDFLARE_ZONE_ID=

# =============================================================================
# THE TOON DEVNET PRESET — the relay and the settlement chains
# =============================================================================
# Where this gateway reads and what its connector settles in. Every value below
# is the TOON devnet's: its relay, and mock USDC on Base Sepolia and on Solana
# devnet — test money. Keep the block as-is to front devnet workloads; to run
# on another network, change the block as a whole: the relay and each token
# are facts about that network, not preferences.

# ── The relay (devnet preset) ────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Where this gateway READS, comma-separated `ws://` or `wss://`. It reads
# exactly two things, both downstream of a handover it has already admitted:
# the Provider Profiles of the members the handover names, and the Takeovers
# that move a workload between them. It watches for no grants — there are none
# to watch for — and it writes nothing, holds no key and has no account.
GATEWAY_RELAYS=wss://relay-ws.devnet.toonprotocol.dev

# ── Settlement (devnet preset) ───────────────────────────────────────────────
# The handover route is free, so this node is never paid; settlement is here
# so a tenant has a key to open its channel against (connector.toml.template
# says more). The connector proves each value against a live chain at boot: a
# wrong address is a refuse-to-start, not a mispriced node. Read the devnet's
# back from any devnet connector's `GET /ilp` rather than trusting this copy.

# Base Sepolia. The TokenNetworkRegistry, not a token network: the connector
# resolves the network through it at boot. Devnet USDC (Circle FiatToken v2.2,
# connector#1337); its decimals must be
# what the token's own decimals() answers.
SETTLEMENT_EVM_RPC_URL=https://base-sepolia-rpc.publicnode.com
SETTLEMENT_EVM_REGISTRY=0x0c41D9D424d6B075A3cEa1068a694f7847a8CCa5
SETTLEMENT_EVM_TOKEN=0x0C996d7c934c79a6255254875607Fe69df25C0E1
SETTLEMENT_EVM_DECIMALS=6

# Solana devnet: the payment-channel program and mock USDC.
SETTLEMENT_SOLANA_RPC_URL=https://api.devnet.solana.com
SETTLEMENT_SOLANA_PROGRAM_ID=2aEVJ8koKD8LTZrLRSGtAtU7LBt4e7QjjCgf1kzQ7Rip
SETTLEMENT_SOLANA_TOKEN=34eSxY7qxQ4GzyhDJ8GpUcTz1WWzruGbJbR8q6TtxfQU
SETTLEMENT_SOLANA_DECIMALS=6

# =============================================================================
# End of the devnet preset.
# =============================================================================

# ── Required: the operator surface's two credentials ─────────────────────────

# Gates the connector's /metrics and redeem endpoints. Any random secret;
# `./keys.sh init` generates one when this is empty.
# Rotate it by changing it here, re-running ./render.sh and restarting the
# connector (the config is read once at startup).
OPERATOR_BEARER_TOKEN=

# The ED25519 PUBLIC key permitted to sign operator writes — 64 hex
# characters, and NOT a nostr npub, a secp256k1 key or base58. When this is
# empty, `./keys.sh init` generates a pair, writes the public half here and
# prints the private half ONCE, storing it nowhere on this box: save it on the
# machine you administer from. To use a key you already hold, put its public
# half here instead, as `connector send --operator-key <file> --print-keyid`
# prints it.
#
# Revoke a key by changing this line, re-rendering and restarting.
OPERATOR_WRITE_KEY=

# =============================================================================
# RUNNING BEHIND THE SHARED EDGE (optional — toon-protocol/gateway#18)
# =============================================================================
# The devnet is moving onto one Linode, behind one Caddy that owns 80 and 443
# for every node on the box (toon-protocol/infra#24, infra ADR 0001). This
# box's own nginx and certbot step aside for it; everything else — the
# connector, the keys, ILP_ADDRESS, GATEWAY_DOMAIN, EDGE_HOST — is unchanged.
#
# The switch, and the compose overlay that goes with it. They are two lines
# because docker compose reads COMPOSE_FILE itself; render.sh refuses a .env
# where they disagree.
# SHARED_EDGE=1
# COMPOSE_FILE=docker-compose.yml:docker-compose.shared-edge.yml
#
# With SHARED_EDGE=1: DNS_PROVIDER and its <PROVIDER>_* lines, and
# LETSENCRYPT_EMAIL and LETSENCRYPT_STAGING, above are all ignored — no
# certificate is issued on this box. deploy/README.md § "Running behind the
# shared edge" has the alias:port table the host's edge is configured from,
# and what its nginx does beyond plain proxying that the edge must replicate.

# ── Optional ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

# ONLY the TOON fleet's own boxes set this. It lets ILP_ADDRESS sit under
# `g.toon.`, the fleet's namespace; anyone else doing so would answer for the
# fleet's handover route and unseal handovers meant for another gateway. The
# devnet gateway box sets TOON_DEVNET_BOX=1, ILP_ADDRESS=g.toon.workload-gateway
# and DNS_PROVIDER=porkbun.
# TOON_DEVNET_BOX=1

# The branch this box follows. `auto-apply.sh` fast-forwards it every five
# minutes and applies what it finds. `main` is the default and is what a
# devnet box should be on; the variable exists so a box can be parked on a
# milestone branch during a bring-up, and because a box silently following a
# branch that does not exist would report success every five minutes while
# sitting on whatever it was last deployed with. auto-apply.sh refuses that
# case by name. Leave it at `main`: nothing an operator customises is a
# committed file, so there is nothing to fork for.
# TRACK_BRANCH=main

# An existing certificate lineage to keep using, if this box already has one
# filed under a different name. Defaults to ${GATEWAY_DOMAIN}.
# CERT_NAME=

# How many admission rounds any one provider may be asked for in a minute.
# Anyone can seal a handover, so this bounds the `status` traffic a stranger's
# packets can make this gateway send. The gateway's own default is 6.
# GATEWAY_ADMIT_PER_MINUTE=6

# The buyer-side SOCKS proxy for members at `.anyone` addresses (spec §10,
# ADR 0008). Only VALIDATED at startup — nothing is dialled until a handover
# names a hidden member — so leaving it empty is safe; a hidden member is then
# refused `no_proxy` rather than quietly dialled in the clear. `socks5h`,
# never `socks5`: the daemon must resolve the name, so it never enters a DNS
# query. This box runs no anon daemon today.
# TOON_SOCKS_PROXY=socks5h://anon:9050
